### 🐦 X / Twitter (The "Punchy Thread" Angle)

**Strategy:** X rewards contrast and quick hits. A short 3-part thread works best here.

**Tweet 1:** API tutorials: "Use nouns instead of verbs! Return 201 Created!"

Production reality: N+1 queries just melted the database, a network timeout double-charged a user, and a missing version header broke 3 client apps. 🧵👇

**Tweet 2:** I wrote down the 5 API design tips I wish someone taught me earlier.

1. Kill N+1 queries (batch your fetches)
    
2. Paginate lists (Cursor > Offset for feeds)
    
3. Idempotency keys (crucial for mutating endpoints)
    
4. RFC 9457 (Structured errors)
    
5. /v1/ from Day One
    

**Tweet 3:** A good API makes the right thing easy and the wrong thing hard.

If you are building backends, stop returning `{ "message": "error" }` and read this: [Link to your blog post]